WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.200 line:95%,end
I talked to a few people.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.600 line:95%,end
I decided it was time to join something bigger.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.400 line:95%,end
And I talked to a couple of different organisations.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:21.800 line:95%,end
I think the approach PubliX seemed to have – Marcus and Alex, and the conversations I've had with them –

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.950 line:95%,end
it felt like the right fit, that it was supportive,

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.950 line:95%,end
that we could continue being Elected Technologies, but as part of a wider thing,

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.900 line:95%,end
rather than be absorbed into something else

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.300 line:95%,end
and just become a product at the end of a set of slides, if you see what I mean.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.250 line:95%,end
With some organisations, you join a bigger company

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.750 line:95%,end
and you're just a logo at the bottom of the website,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.100 line:95%,end
or a product that's referenced on slide 72,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:01.450 line:95%,end
or something for the sales team to reach for if they need to,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.400 line:95%,end
if they think you match an existing client.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.600 line:95%,end
And I just found that we get the support to continue to grow,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.300 line:95%,end
at a stage where, as I said, I think we've hit a certain level.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.250 line:95%,end
And it'll enable us to go further,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.950 line:95%,end
but in a way that still lets us be the company that we are.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:29.850 line:95%,end
And a lot of consolidator groups – it feels a bit like PE, financial engineering:

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.300 line:95%,end
consolidate these together, reduce these costs,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.900 line:95%,end
follow this cookie-cutter plan that we've had before.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:44.500 line:95%,end
And then the PE firm's number goes up, and yours goes up as well.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.300 line:95%,end
The other thing that attracted me to PubliX was the chance to reinvest into the group.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:55.100 line:95%,end
So being part of something that becomes bigger, more than the sum of its parts,

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.950 line:95%,end
rather than just cash out, stick around for a few years, and then that's it.
